# A ring (radii 5 and 2) cut through a 10-high block from its side, its outer circle tangent to
# the block's top and bottom: the two sides left meet only along the tangent lines, a non-manifold
# result, refused as ZeroThickness there (the owner's decision, as mainstream mechanical CAD).
# Onshape builds a CADFS part (00850232) of this form. A ring of radius 4 builds.
sketch base(on: xy) {
  o = rect(corner: (0, 0), size: (30, 20))
}
block = extrude(base, 10)
sketch ring(on: block.side(base.o[3])) {
  a = circle((5, 5), 5)
  b = circle((5, 5), 2)
}
tube = cut(ring, upto(block.side(base.o[1])))
